[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "doc-90-docs-business-cloud-itonami-flagship-generator-template", :doc/title "cloud-itonami flagship checklist item 2 — reusable build-time-demo generator template", :doc/path "90-docs/business/cloud-itonami-flagship-generator-template.edn", :doc/body "# cloud-itonami flagship checklist item 2 — reusable generator template\n\n**As-of**: 2026-07-19 (Wave5 rollout iteration 6, ADR-2607189300 ledger seq 6)\n**Template files**: `90-docs/business/scripts/flagship-generator-template/{render_html.clj.template,regenerate.yml.template}`\n**Proven on**: `cloud-itonami-isic-851` (schoolops), `cloud-itonami-isic-6820` (realty)\n\n## Why this exists\n\nWave5 iteration 5 found the isic-6399/6310/7810 \"port `regenerate.yml`\n onto an existing `web/generate.cljs`\" playbook had run out of targets:\nonly those 3 repos (of 1,109 scanned) had any generator script at all,\nand 930/1,109 (84%) had no demo file whatsoever. The ledger concluded\nevery further repo would need a bespoke, from-scratch build-time\nrenderer (the isic-2910/`automotive.render-html` pattern, ledger seq 4)\n-- roughly one iteration of work each, too slow to make a dent in 930\nrepos at 30-minute-iteration granularity. Iteration 6 tested whether a\nREUSABLE template could cut that marginal cost, instead of assuming\neither that it would (premature abstraction) or wouldn't (giving up\nwithout evidence).\n\n## Homogeneity evidence (measured, not assumed)\n\nSampled 13 repos from the \"no demo, no generator\" bucket spanning\nunrelated ISIC sectors (agriculture 0111, food-manufacture 1040,\nchemicals 2011, utilities 3511, retail 4721, accommodation 5520,\nsoftware 6201, real-estate 6820, research 7210, education 851,\nhealth 861, membership-orgs 941, personal-care 960). Findings:\n\n- 11/13 shared the identical `src/<domain>/{facts,phase,sim,governor,\n  operation,advisor,store}.cljc` + root `deps.edn` shape, no `web/`\n  dir, no `http.clj` -- the same shape `cloud-itonami-isic-2910`\n  (already fixed, ledger seq 4) has. 2 outliers: `isic-2011` is a\n  blueprint-only stub (empty `src/`, a different maturity tier\n  entirely -- no actor to drive yet); `isic-6201` is a Ring-HTTP-served\n  CRM-fleet sibling (`http.clj`, shares `kotoba-lang/crm` with\n  isic-5820/6202/6209) -- a genuinely different, smaller cluster.\n- A full filesystem pass (no cloning needed, `orgs/cloud-itonami/`\n  already checked out) over all 1,109 real local checkouts confirmed\n  this at scale: **363/1,109 (33%)** match the shape signature\n  mechanically (single `src/<domain>/` dir with `operation.cljc` +\n  `governor.cljc` + `store.cljc`, root `deps.edn`, no `package.json`,\n  no `web/`, no `http.clj`). Of those, **290/1,109 (26% of the whole\n  fleet)** additionally have a REAL `langgraph.graph` StateGraph in\n  `operation.cljc` (`g/state-graph`/`g/add-node`/`g/compile-graph`) --\n  confirmed by grep, not inferred. The remaining ~290/1,109 (26%) are\n  stub/empty (`290 empty-or-no-src`, an earlier maturity tier, no actor\n  to render from at all); ~456/1,109 (41%) are structurally \"other\"\n  (multi-domain repos, HTTP-service repos, or a `build` stub without a\n  real StateGraph -- e.g. `isic-0111`/`isic-1040`'s `run-operation`\n  pattern, ~26 repos sampled-checked, mirrors an older `cattleops`-\n  style template generation the fleet moved on from).\n- Spot-checked node/channel naming across 8 of the 290 (isic-2910,\n  4721, 5520, 6820, 7210, 851, 861, 3511): **100% identical** --\n  channels `:request :context :proposal :verdict :disposition :record\n  :approval :audit`, nodes `:intake :advise :govern :decide\n  :request-approval :commit :hold`, `:interrupt-before\n  #{:request-approval}`, entry point `:intake`, finish points\n  `:commit`/`:hold`. This is not coincidence -- the whole fleet was\n  code-generated from one shared blueprint, so the INVOCATION HARNESS\n  (`exec!`/`approve!` via `g/run*` with `:thread-id`) is copy-pasteable\n  **verbatim** across all 290 repos; only the demo scenario (domain-\n  specific request maps) and the rendering table (domain-specific\n  entity fields) are genuinely per-repo.\n\n**Conclusion**: the 290-repo cluster (26% of the fleet) is real,\nlarge, and homogeneous enough to justify a template. It is NOT the\nmajority of the full 1,109-repo fleet (33% total shape-A, of which 290\nhave the real StateGraph; the other ~74% needs different treatment or\nis pre-actor), so this is reported as a well-defined SUB-CLUSTER win,\nnot a fleet-wide one -- consistent with this rollout's guardrail\nagainst forcing one abstraction over genuinely heterogeneous ground.\n\n## What the template is (and isn't)\n\nNOT a shared library dependency (`deps.edn` `:local/root`) -- every\nrepo in this fleet is deliberately standalone/forkable (see e.g.\n`isic-0111`'s own deps.edn docstring), and introducing a shared\n`ops-scaffold` dependency between vertical repos would break that\ninvariant the same way the fleet's own duplicated `operation.cljc`/\n`governor.cljc` pattern deliberately does NOT share a library either.\nInstead it is a COPY-AND-ADAPT source template (same spirit as\niterations 1/2's `regenerate.yml` porting): `render_html.clj.template`\nhas 4 explicitly marked ADAPT points (namespace requires, cosmetic\nactor-role label, the demo scenario itself, and the subject-key field\nname used in ledger facts -- confirmed to vary: `:subject` in\nisic-6820/isic-2910, `:student-id` in isic-851, `:field-id` in the\nolder cerealops-style stub repos); the harness fns (`exec!`/`approve!`)\nand the HTML/CSS shell are copy-verbatim. `regenerate.yml.template`\nneeds only a repo-name find/replace (4 occurrences) + a domain-ns\nfind/replace (1 occurrence).\n\n**Adopting this template still requires reading the target repo's own\n`store.cljc` (for real seed-data ids) and `governor.cljc` (for the real\nclosed op-allowlist / hard-violation reasons) and writing a genuine\nscenario against them** -- it is not zero-touch, but it turns\n\"author a build-time renderer from scratch\" (the isic-2910 pattern,\n~1 iteration) into \"fill in 4 marked blanks using real data already in\nthe repo\" (demonstrated at ~15-20 min/repo once the template existed,\nvs. the from-scratch estimate).\n\n**Known trap this template documents explicitly**: a target repo's own\n`sim.cljc` demo driver is not automatically trustworthy as a scenario\nsource. `isic-851`'s `schoolops.sim` turned out to be a latent,\npre-existing bug -- copy-pasted from an unrelated eldercare (ISIC-873)\nactor, it drives requests against ids (`resident-1`) that don't exist\nin schoolops' own seeded data (`student-1`/`student-2`/`student-3`),\nso every one of its calls actually HARD-holds on `:student-unverified`\nregardless of which \"happy path\" its own comments claim to demonstrate\n-- confirmed by running `clojure -M:dev:run` directly, not assumed.\n`isic-6820`'s own `realty.sim`, by contrast, was correct and safe to\nmine directly. The template's own header comment now tells future\nporters to verify this per-repo rather than trust it.\n\n**No kotoba-ui / shitsuke.hig design-system integration**: these are\nstandalone, forkable, pure-JVM-Clojure repos with zero npm/cljs/\nreagent toolchain (`clojure -M` only) -- `kotoba-ui.core`'s\nSSR-via-reagent-seam pipeline assumes a JS/npm build step these repos\ndeliberately don't have. Followed the existing `cloud-itonami-isic-2910`\nprecedent instead (ledger seq 4): a single inline `<style>` block with\nsemantically-named CSS classes (`.ok`/`.warn`/`.err`/`.critical`/\n`.muted`), defined once, not scattered ad-hoc hex through the markup --\nthe spirit of \"one definition point per semantic meaning\" without\nforcing an architecturally-mismatched dependency into a zero-JS repo.\nNoted here plainly per this rollout's honesty discipline, not silently\nglossed over.\n\n## Applied this iteration (ledger seq 6)\n\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-851` (primary-education back-office coordination):\n  `src/schoolops/render_html.clj` + `:render-html` deps.edn alias +\n  `.github/workflows/regenerate.yml`. Scenario: student-1 clears 4\n  phase-3-auto ops + 1 always-escalate safety-concern flag (approved);\n  student-3 (unverified) and student-2 (scope-excluded content) both\n  HARD-hold, never reaching a human.\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-6820` (real-estate fee-services): adapted\n  `src/realty/render_html.clj` from this repo's own (verified-correct)\n  `realty.sim` scenario -- a full intake->assess->file->pay lifecycle\n  on property-1, a contract execution on property-4, and 3 distinct\n  HARD holds (no-spec-basis, fee-for-unmanaged-property,\n  contract-exceeds-authorization-limit).\n\nBoth: verified locally (real actor output), idempotent (byte-identical\nreruns, confirmed via sha256 diff), byte-identical under a from-scratch\nCI-layout simulation, no test regressions, merged via GitHub API\nserver-side merge, verified via a live `workflow_dispatch` run to\n`conclusion=success` with the run's own `commit when changed` step\nlogging `console unchanged` (confirming CI's independent regeneration\nbyte-matches the merged commit), and confirmed via the live GitHub\nPages URL serving the new build-time-generated content. See\nADR-2607189300 ledger seq 6 for exact commit SHAs and run URLs.\n\n## What this does NOT claim\n\n- Does not claim the other ~64% of the fleet (290 empty/stub + 456\n  \"other\") is covered by this or any template -- explicitly flagged as\n  a separate, still-unsolved body of work.\n- Does not promote isic-851 or isic-6820 to the flagship cohort\n  (`cloud-itonami-vertical-maturity.edn`) -- that is a separate,\n  larger decision (checklist items 1/3/5/6/7 not evaluated this\n  iteration) this iteration did not make.\n- The ~26 `run-operation`/`build`-stub repos (isic-0111/1040-style,\n  an older non-StateGraph pattern) are a further, smaller candidate\n  sub-cluster for a SEPARATE template variant -- not attempted this\n  iteration, flagged as a follow-up.\n\n## Related\n\n- `90-docs/adr/2607189300-cloud-itonami-flagship-wave5-all-repo-rollout-tracking.edn`\n- `90-docs/business/cloud-itonami-flagship-rollout-ledger.edn` seq 4 (isic-2910, the pattern this template was extracted from), seq 5 (fleet-wide scanner), seq 6 (this template + its 2 proof repos)\n- `90-docs/business/cloud-itonami-flagship-checklist-scan.edn` (generated fleet scan)\n", :doc/source-format "edn", :doc/doc_type "doc"}]
